      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An unusual late complication of bacterial endocarditis is described. Four years after diagnosis and treatment, a patient is seen with coronary artery compression caused by a large pseudoaneurysm of the mitral-aortic intervalvular fibrosa. The utility of transesophageal echocardiography in diagnosis and surgical management is emphasized."},
